flowchart TB
  accTitle: Autonomous Repository Template architecture
  accDescr: A human request goes through setup scripts that instantiate or adopt a product repository. In the default supervised profile, a plan records one human-approved milestone, a coding agent such as Claude Code, Codex, or Cursor implements it, the project's own checks run, and the work comes back as local commits and a handoff for human review. The opt-in lite and full profiles add a planning gate check, verification cycles, and tracked state under .ai.

  human(["`**Human**
  request, approval, review`"])
  scripts["`**Setup scripts**
  instantiate, adopt, switch`"]

  subgraph repo["PRODUCT REPOSITORY · SUPERVISED"]
    plan["`**Plan**
    one approved milestone`"]
    agent["`**Coding agent**
    Claude Code, Codex, Cursor`"]
    checks["`**Project checks**
    listed in the plan`"]
    handoff["`**Handoff**
    local commits + notes`"]
  end

  legacy["`**Lite / full profiles** · opt-in
  planning gate, verification cycles,
  tracked .ai/ state`"]

  human -->|request| scripts
  scripts --> plan
  human -->|approves| plan
  plan ==> agent
  agent ==> checks
  checks ==>|for human review| handoff
  plan -.-> legacy

  classDef key fill:#e6eee9,stroke:#315e55,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#192c32
  classDef ext fill:#f7f8f5,stroke:#7c8f83,color:#192c32
  classDef side fill:#f7f8f5,stroke:#b6c3ba,stroke-dasharray:6 4,color:#526460
  class plan key
  class legacy side
